WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.949 --> 00:00:08.910
Caroline Aghajanian: On this
episode of "Travel Dares,"

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.580
I'm taking Nico to Retro,

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.580
where we're gonna make
Georgia's largest khachapuri.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.030
Nico Reyes: And I'm taking
Caroline to Sam Raan Spa,

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.010
where we're gonna try

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.150
a traditional hammam bubble treatment.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.830
Caroline: Come join us on our adventures

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.013
on this episode of "Travel Dares."

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.530
This is "Travel Dares,"

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.420
the show where we do daring
activities all over Europe

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.130
empowered by my Marriott
Bonvoy Boundless card.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.530
Nico: In this episode,
we're in Tbilisi, Georgia,

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:37.810
and we're so excited

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.000
to check out the cuisine and the culture.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.173
Ready for your clue, Caroline?

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:42.660
Caroline: Yes, let's get started!

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:43.493
OK.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.232
Nico: Think about it.

00:00:48.232 --> 00:00:50.430
Caroline: I'm thinking, I don't know.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.470
Swimming?

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:52.385
Nico: Possibly.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.302
Caroline: Possibly?

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.480
I feel like we're going on a,

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.288
like, a lazy river ride or something.

00:00:58.288 --> 00:00:59.646
You know?
Nico: A lazy river ride?

00:00:59.646 --> 00:01:02.760
Traditional hammam spas
are iconic to this region,

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.160
and they include a section

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.430
where you are covered in bubbles.

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:08.510
Caroline and I have
tried beauty treatments

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:09.970
from all over the world,

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.450
so I know she's gonna love this one.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:15.590
Reach this hand down,
down, down, and scoop.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.732
Are you scooping?

00:01:16.732 --> 00:01:18.560
Caroline: I'm scooping, what is it?

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.357
Nico: Take off your blindfold,

00:01:20.357 --> 00:01:22.403
'cause today we're doing a traditional

00:01:22.403 --> 00:01:23.671
hammam bubble treatment.

00:01:23.671 --> 00:01:24.524
Caroline: Bubble bath!

00:01:24.524 --> 00:01:25.357
Nico: Yes!

00:01:25.357 --> 00:01:26.513
Caroline: Oh, my God!

00:01:26.513 --> 00:01:29.013
Nico: This is the dare
we've been waiting for.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.620
Oh, my gosh!

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:40.941
Caroline: Oh, my gosh.

00:01:40.941 --> 00:01:42.670
Oh, it is instantly so much warmer.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:45.005
Nico: It feels so warm in here.

00:01:45.005 --> 00:01:46.250
Caroline: I'm gonna cry.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.460
I feel like a queen walking
into her weekly bath.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.500
Let's just lay down, I guess.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.956
Oh, this is so luxurious.

00:01:53.956 --> 00:01:55.740
I'm not used to it.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.680
Ihga: Hammam is an ancient ritual.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.150
Ottomans brought their
own bathing tradition

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:03.300
to Constantinople in 15th century.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.350
Hammam meaning is the
"spreader of warmth."

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.460
It's a rejuvenating procedure

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.560
leaving you feeling
refreshed inside and out.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.018
Caroline: So, we don't
even go to the bubble bath.

00:02:13.018 --> 00:02:14.995
The bubbles come to us.

00:02:14.995 --> 00:02:18.270
Nico: Oh. Oh, it's happening. Oh, my God!

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.620
Caroline: Oh, my gosh!

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:22.260
I love these bubbles!

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.250
There's so much bubbles!

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:25.431
Nico: I'm making bubble snow angels.

00:02:25.431 --> 00:02:27.422
Caroline: Oh, my gosh.

00:02:27.422 --> 00:02:28.560
Wow.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.850
I'm drowning in these bubbles.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.620
Ihga: Hammam positively affects

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.430
on different body functions.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.410
Physical and emotional detox,

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:39.090
cleans skin pores of impurities

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.350
and sloughs the dead skin, pain relief,

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:45.490
muscle relaxation, relieves some stresses,

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.240
boost the immune system,

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.150
and giving you unforgettable feeling.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:54.090
Caroline: My skin feels silky smooth.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:55.678
Nico: Every time I rub in the bubbles,

00:02:55.678 --> 00:02:57.890
it just feels softer and softer.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:58.910
Caroline: I definitely think

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:00.850
out of all the spas I've ever been to,

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:02.160
this one is my favorite.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.748
Nico, I have a little surprise for you.

00:03:05.748 --> 00:03:07.196
Nico: No.

00:03:07.196 --> 00:03:08.368
Caroline: [laughs] I have the clue.

00:03:08.368 --> 00:03:10.940
Nico: What the heck, where
were you keeping this?

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.860
I was just getting relaxed.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.888
Oh, it's soggy.

00:03:15.888 --> 00:03:17.799
[Caroline laughs]

00:03:21.753 --> 00:03:23.240
Caroline: All right, so I'll blindfold you

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.740
once we get these bubbles off.

00:03:34.423 --> 00:03:35.473
Nico: I don't know.

00:03:35.473 --> 00:03:38.020
I don't know any non-floating boats.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:39.820
Every boat that I've met floats.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.930
Caroline: Khachapuri is
an iconic Georgian dish

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.530
consisting of egg, cheese, and bread.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:45.700
Retro is known to make

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.860
one of the largest
khachapuri in the world,

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.250
and chef Gia is gonna
teach us how to make it.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.260
And now stop here.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:52.230
Nico: Oh, OK.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.120
Caroline: Perfect.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.000
All right, smell what this is.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:58.383
Nico: I don't know.

00:03:58.383 --> 00:04:00.378
It smells like a pastry?

00:04:00.378 --> 00:04:01.211
Caroline: OK.

00:04:01.211 --> 00:04:02.600
Nico: Like a cheesy pastry?

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.130
Caroline: Yes, so take your blindfold off,

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:08.123
because today we're learning
how to make khachapuri,

00:04:08.123 --> 00:04:11.012
aka a Georgian cheese boat.

00:04:11.012 --> 00:04:12.690
Nico: "This boat won't float"!

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:13.523
Caroline: Yes.

00:04:13.523 --> 00:04:14.906
Nico: It makes sense now.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.894
Sali: This is Gia.
Caroline: Hello, chef!

00:04:23.894 --> 00:04:24.827
Gia Agirba: Gia. Hello, hello.

00:04:24.827 --> 00:04:25.660
Caroline: It's so nice to meet you!

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:26.510
Nico: Hello, nice to meet you.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:27.618
Sali: Today, I will be your translator.

00:04:27.618 --> 00:04:29.440
So, let's start making khachapuri.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.510
Nico: Yay!

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:32.977
Caroline: Nico, I do
have a surprise for you.

00:04:32.977 --> 00:04:34.990
We're not just making khachapuri;

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:38.470
we're making an
over-5-foot-long khachapuri.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:40.629
Nico: Oh, my gosh!

00:04:40.629 --> 00:04:42.720
That's why there's so much dough?

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:43.997
Caroline: Nico, are you ready to do this?

00:04:43.997 --> 00:04:45.781
Nico: Yes, I'm so psyched.

00:04:59.187 --> 00:05:00.565
Gia: Georgia mozzarella.

00:05:00.565 --> 00:05:03.640
Nico and Caroline: Oh, Georgia mozzarella!

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:05.557
Nico: It looks so good!

00:05:08.526 --> 00:05:10.640
Caroline: Nico, all your eggs are runny.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:12.340
Nico: Two of my eggs ran.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.206
Caroline: It has to be perfect.

00:05:23.799 --> 00:05:24.632
Caroline: Oh, my God.

00:05:24.632 --> 00:05:26.482
Gia: Super!
Caroline: Yes, super.

00:05:26.482 --> 00:05:28.290
We just made the Titanic.

00:05:35.912 --> 00:05:36.745
Caroline: We made that!

00:05:36.745 --> 00:05:37.887
Gia: We've done it! We've done it!

00:05:37.887 --> 00:05:39.207
Caroline: Got it, got it.

00:05:39.207 --> 00:05:40.855
Nico: I'm coming in, coming in.

00:05:40.855 --> 00:05:43.241
Ooh, it's hot, it's hot.

00:05:43.241 --> 00:05:45.860
[clapping and cheering]

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.850
Sali: So, girls, next step is
to mix in everything together.

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:50.348
Nico: Oh, the butter!

00:05:50.348 --> 00:05:51.605
Caroline: I know, it smells really good.

00:05:51.605 --> 00:05:53.240
Nico: The butter smells so good.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:54.718
Sali: Caroline, please.
Caroline: Yes.

00:05:54.718 --> 00:05:55.889
[all laughing]

00:05:55.889 --> 00:05:57.722
Sali: One, two, three!

00:05:59.738 --> 00:06:00.730
Oh, my God.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.222
Nico: Is it good?
Caroline: It's so good.

00:06:02.222 --> 00:06:03.788
Sali: Nico, now it's your turn.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:05.563
Sali: How is it?

00:06:05.563 --> 00:06:08.350
Nico: Oh, my God, that is so good!

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:11.000
It's so creamy and delicious and rich

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.500
because of all that cheese.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.840
It's so good.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:15.214
Caroline: Now we know why they call you

00:06:15.214 --> 00:06:18.040
the best in Georgia, OK.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:18.873
We did it!

00:06:18.873 --> 00:06:19.994
Nico: We did it!
Caroline: We did it!

00:06:19.994 --> 00:06:23.234
Gmadlobt, chef Gia! Thank you so much!

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:24.524
Nico and Caroline: Bye!

00:06:24.524 --> 00:06:26.090
Gia: Thank you.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:27.880
Nico: Caroline, that was so delicious.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.489
Caroline: I know.

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:38.470
Nico: Out of all the
places we've traveled to,

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.000
Georgia is so unique.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.830
Caroline: I know. I
loved staying in Tbilisi.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.210
It has such a rich history.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.950
Like, this hotel was constructed in 1910,

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:49.330
and it's the first European
standard hotel in Tbilisi.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:50.997
Nico: Caroline, let's talk bubbles.

00:06:50.997 --> 00:06:51.830
Caroline: Bubbles!

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:53.640
Nico: I think you did a really good job

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.870
of staying really positive and relaxed

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:57.240
throughout the whole process,

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.540
even when your skin was being scrubbed.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:00.640
You did a really good job,

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:01.890
so I'll give you five stars.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:02.990
Caroline: Yes!

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:05.490
I loved it. I had such an amazing time,

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:08.390
and my skin feels so soft.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.360
So, making that giant khachapuri

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:13.250
requires a lot of skill
and a lot of speed,

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.850
and I'm so glad we didn't drop it

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:16.870
when we were taking it out of the oven.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.080
But we were a little slow

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:21.240
during the preparation
process, especially the eggs.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.010
That was a little frantic.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:26.134
So for that, I'm giving
you a 4.5 out of five.

00:07:26.134 --> 00:07:27.742
Nico: 4.5?

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.130
I guess that's fair.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.010
That's fair.

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:32.450
Caroline: Yeah, it was still so delicious.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:33.283
Nico: Yeah.

00:07:33.283 --> 00:07:34.796
Caroline: Georgia was amazing,

00:07:34.796 --> 00:07:36.104
but now we're about to meet Aj

00:07:36.104 --> 00:07:37.120
in Switzerland,
Nico: Yeah!

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:38.850
and I'm super excited for that.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:40.149
Aj, we're coming for you.

00:07:40.149 --> 00:07:41.301
Nico: We're coming, Aj!

00:07:41.301 --> 00:07:42.976
Caroline: Cheers!
Nico: Cheers!

